<title>USA: Merrill cuts DuPont 1998 EPS outlook.</title>
<headline>Merrill cuts DuPont 1998 EPS outlook.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch said Monday that it had cut DuPont Co's 1998 earnings per share outlook to $3.65 from $3.90 after the company's acquisition of Imperial Chemical Industries Plc's polyester and European and Asian Tioxide businesses.</p>
<p>The financing costs alone from the deal are expected to be $0.10 to $0.15 a share in 1998, the year in which the deal becomes effective, analyst John Roberts said.</p>
<p>DuPont stock was up 3/8 at 63-5/8 by 1054 EDT/1454 GMT, having traded as low at 62-1/4.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
